## ✅ **Step 2: Frontend Integration (React Example)**

### 2.1 Basic Components

```jsx
// ChatApp.jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import axios from 'axios';

const ChatApp = () => {
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);
  const [input, setInput] = useState('');

  const sendMessage = async () => {
    if (!input.trim()) return;

    const newMessage = { role: 'user', text: input };
    setMessages([...messages, newMessage]);

    try {
      const res = await axios.post('http://localhost:5000/chat', { message: input });
      const reply = {
        role: res.data.type === 'ai' ? 'ai' : 'reminder',
        text: res.data.message,
      };
      setMessages((msgs) => [...msgs, reply]);
      setInput('');
    } catch (err) {
      console.error(err);
    }
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ padding: 20 }}>
      <h2>Chat with Reminder AI</h2>
      <div style={{ height: 300, overflowY: 'auto', border: '1px solid #ccc', padding: 10 }}>
        {messages.map((msg, i) => (
          <div key={i} style={{ margin: '10px 0', textAlign: msg.role === 'user' ? 'right' : 'left' }}>
            <b>{msg.role === 'user' ? 'You' : (msg.role === 'reminder' ? '📅 ReminderBot' : '🤖 ChatGPT')}:</b> {msg.text}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <input
        value={input}
        onChange={(e) => setInput(e.target.value)}
        placeholder="Type a message..."
        style={{ width: '80%' }}
      />
      <button onClick={sendMessage} style={{ width: '18%' }}>Send</button>
    </div>
  );
};

export default ChatApp;
```

---

## ✅ **Result**

* When the user says something like **"Remind me to call John at 8 PM"**, `chrono-node` detects the time, and the app confirms: **"Reminder set for \[DateTime]"**.
* If no time is found, the query is sent to ChatGPT and the response is shown.
